<title>HONG KONG: Gilbert interim net rises 15 percent.</title>
<headline>Gilbert interim net rises 15 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   4.1    vs  4.8 (see note)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    2.0    vs  nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs  nil</p>
<p>    Net			    14.40  vs  12.51</p>
<p>    Turnover		     282.18 vs  249.66</p>
<p>    Company name		 Gilbert Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  January 27-31, 1997</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   February 5</p>
<p>NOTE - Gilbert Holdings is a flax trader.</p>
<p>Share earnings are based on the weighted average of 350 million shares vs 262.50 million.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
